s question therefore changed the active build\\\\u2019s HEAD and invalidated an otherwise executor-authored build. The green forge checks do not cure this race, and the selected-test failure does not explain the recorded refusal.\\\\n\\\\n## Retires\\\\n\\\\nA read-only counsel/status inquiry, or transport of its record, being able to introduce a foreign commit into an active build\\\\u2019s commit range.\\\\n\\\\n## Change\\\\n\\\\nMake counsel/status recording and transport unable to mutate the checkout observed by an active build. Use an isolated transport worktree or defer the counsel-record commit until the active stage has produced its record. Preserve the build\\\\u2019s foreign-author guard; driver commits must not be silently exempted from it.\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance\\\\n\\\\n- Start a two-iteration build whose first iteration creates an executor-authored commit and whose second iteration is still running.\\\\n- Run `attavo counsel N --ask \\\\\\\"how is it going so far?\\\\\\\"` and transport its record during that interval.\\\\n- The active build\\\\u2019s HEAD and executor commit range remain unchanged by the counsel operation.\\\\n- The build is not refused for the counsel record and can pass after its gates pass.\\\\n- The counsel record is eventually committed by the driver without being lost.\\\\n- An actual non-executor commit introduced into the build\\\\u2019s range remains refused by the existing authorship guard.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"forge\\\": {\\n    \\\"read\\\": true,\\n    \\\"reason\\\": null,\\n    \\\"checks\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"coherence\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"schema-version\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"action-self-check\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"spec-gate\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"doctor\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"test\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"typecheck\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"what is your recommendation?\\\",\\n  \\\"record_version\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"item\\\": \\\"229\\\",\\n  \\\"product_version\\\": \\\"v0.29.0-10-gdae6d76\\\",\\n  \\\"product_pin\\\": \\\"v0.29.0\\\"\\n}\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:20:STOP_CLASSES = (\\\"non-question\\\", \\\"outlived-invocation\\\", \\\"no-cause\\\", \\\"forge-unconcluded\\\",\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:21:               \\\"ceiling\\\", \\\"claims-boundary\\\", \\\"repeated-act\\\", \\\"unclassed\\\", \\\"question\\\",\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:47:# moves non-question and outlived-invocation onto report_class instead\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:48:# (below): non-question's own halt line (\\\"halted: class non-question\\\")\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:55:    \\\"non-question\\\": (),\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:67:    # judgment like non-question/outlived-invocation are. Left at the\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:74:    # A genuine question (issue #100's own followups) is read structurally\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:75:    # -- status \\\"halted\\\" carrying a non-empty halted.question -- not by\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:76:    # scanning for the literal word \\\"question\\\", which the question's own\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:79:    # question that happens to use the word \\\"question\\\" as executor\\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:81:    \\\"question\\\": (),\\n/Users/d